<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n96054" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπονδο-φόρος</span></b> , ὁ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who offers
			libations</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.683
			</span></i>:—hence, <i>one who brings proposals for a
			truce</i> or <i>treaty of peace</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				216
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>herald</i> or <i>officer who published the</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπονδαί</span> of the Olympic and other
			games, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπονδοφόροι Ζηνὸς Ἀλεῖοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>I.</u>
					2.23
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ς. οἱ τὰς μυστηριώτιδας σπονδὰς
					ἐπαγγέλλοντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					2.133
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				1021.7
			</span></i> (Olympia, <span class="entity">i B.C.</span>), al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			= Lat. <i>fetialis</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				1.21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.279b
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
